{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":45},"timestamp":1790148745,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":".venv/bin/cortex-ask --real --tenant █████████ \"can i trust our crm data? what is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\"","title":"real_crm_trust","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: can i trust our crm data? what is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-23 13:02:27\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  1.1s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  1.1s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  1.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  1.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [  5.3s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 12.1s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 12.1s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 12.1s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 12.1s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 12.1s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 13.9s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 13.9s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 13.9s] step 1   got hubspot__search (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 13.9s] step 1   got hubspot__search (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 13.9s] step 1   got hubspot__search (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 13.9s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 17.1s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 17.1s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 17.1s] step 2   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 19.7s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.7s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (10 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.7s] step 2   got hubspot__activities (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.7s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 24.0s] step 3   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 24.0s] step 3   got read hubspot.companies in full (50 rows) (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 29.1s] step 3   got hubspot__activities (12 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 29.1s] step 4   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 4   got read hubspot.activities in full (50 rows) (12 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.4s] step 5   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 34.9s] step 5   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 34.9s] step 5   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 39.2s] step 5   got hubspot__companies (13 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 39.2s] step 5   got hubspot__companies (14 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 39.2s] step 6   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 41.7s] step 6   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 41.7s] step 6   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 47.0s] step 6   got hubspot__companies (15 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 47.0s] step 6   got hubspot__activities (16 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 47.0s] step 7   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 73.1s]          drafting the report from 16 observation(s)\r\n  [118.8s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [118.8s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (6.0s); missing: Per-deal field-completeness audit across a broader property set (contract dates, deal_type consistency, close reasons) rather than just amount/owner presence checks; Comparison against source \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-of-record (e.g., signed contract dates vs CRM close_date) to check for backdating or sync lag; Historical baseline of data quality in prior quarters to know if current gaps are a change or status quo; Explanation for the company-search anomaly (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 misspelled as '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' in deal name) - whether this is a one-off typo or indicates \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ic naming/sync issues\r\n  [138.5s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Can I trust our CRM data? What is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 119s over 7 steps, 47,097 tokens, 16 observations gathered, 12 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The underlying company database has \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ic duplicate records (multiple entries for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' and repeated entries for other company names), which increases the risk that engagement and contact data for closed-won accounts is fragmented across records rather than genuinely missing.  [hubspot.companies 80c39f4d, hubspot.companies a184977d]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Four deals closed this quarter, all with complete core fields  (high)\r\n    - Between 2026-07-01 and 2026-09-23, four deals closed won, totaling $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588: \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588k, closed 2026-09-18), \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588k, closed 2026-09-04), \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 - Self-hosted (\"$\u2588\u2588\u2588k, closed 2026-08-31), and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588k, closed 2026-08-17).  [hubspot.closed_won 22826304]\r\n    - None of these four deals is missing amount or owner: a search for closed-won deals in this window without an amount returned zero matches, and a search for closed-won deals without an owner also returned zero matches.  [hubspot.search 2c62f3ea, hubspot.search 7401f383]\r\n  Deal names do not match their linked company records for at least two of the four deals  (high)\r\n    - The deal named \"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\" has no matching company record under that spelling; a company search for \"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\" returned zero results, while the correctly-spelled company \"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\" (Luxembourg, legal services, customer lifecycle stage) does exist.  [hubspot.search 09536e3d, hubspot.companies e89a9b89, hubspot.companies cd446a09]\r\n    - The deal named \"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\" does not exactly match its likely company record, \"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\" (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, customer lifecycle stage) \u2014 the deal name is a garbled/misspelled variant of the company name.  [hubspot.search 09536e3d, hubspot.companies 8dfac3d8]\r\n  Widespread duplicate company records for accounts in the closed-won set  (high)\r\n    - A company search for \"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\" returned \u2588 distinct company records under the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 name/domain family, including one record with a null company name and null country despite having a populated domain (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588).  [hubspot.companies a184977d]\r\n  Activity history is inconsistent across accounts of similar deal size \u2014 one $\u2588\u2588\u2588k deal shows no engagement trail at all  (medium)\r\n    - The company record linked to the $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal (id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) has zero logged engagements (emails, calls, meetings) despite the deal having \u2588\u2588 associated contacts and being closed won.  [hubspot.activities c974603c, hubspot.closed_won 22826304]\r\n    - By contrast, the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 account (deal id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) has \u2588\u2588 logged engagements spanning emails, calls, and meetings from June through October \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, and the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 account (deal id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) has \u2588\u2588 logged engagements, mostly emails, from June through September \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588.  [hubspot.activities 290ff245, hubspot.activities 10f35c7d, hubspot.closed_won 22826304]\r\n    - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal's source_detail is \"IMPORT\" while the other three deals show CRM_UI, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, or organic-search source detail, consistent with the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal having been bulk-imported rather than worked through the CRM's normal engagement-logging flow.  [hubspot.closed_won 22826304]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal's missing engagement history is because the deal was imported rather than natively created and tracked in HubSpot.\r\n      The deal's source_detail is literally 'IMPORT', distinguishing it from the other three deals (CRM_UI, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, organic search), and it is the only one of the four with zero engagements despite having the most associated contacts (\u2588\u2588) and the largest amount ($\u2588\u2588\u2588k) \u2014 a size/complexity that would normally generate substantial activity if worked live in the CRM.\r\n  [contradicted] Closed-won deals in this quarter are missing core required fields (amount, owner) that would make the CRM unreliable for revenue reporting.\r\n      Explicit searches for closed-won deals missing amount or missing owner both returned zero matching records, ruling out this as the source of any data-trust concern for this quarter's closed-won set.\r\n  [inconclusive] Deal-name-to-company-record mismatches (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) reflect manual data entry errors rather than a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ic naming convention issue across all deals.\r\n      Only \u2588 of \u2588 deal names were checked against company records and both showed mismatches; this is too small a sample, and no deal-to-company association field was directly inspected, to establish whether this is a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ic issue or isolated to these two records. Ruling on cause would require inspecting the deal-company association records directly, which was not done.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Deduplicate company records for accounts with repeated names, starting with the two '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' records and the eight-plus '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' records, and verify which \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 record the $\u2588\u2588\u2588k closed-won deal is actually associated with.\r\n      why: Duplicate company records for the same account risk splitting engagement history and contact associations across records, which would explain why the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal shows zero engagements on the record inspected \u2014 the activity may be sitting on a duplicate record instead.\r\n      [hubspot.companies 80c39f4d, hubspot.activities c974603c]\r\n  P\u2588 Correct the deal names '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' and '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' to match their company records ('\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' and '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'), and add a validation or lookup step at deal creation to prevent free-text company name entry from diverging from the linked company record.\r\n      why: Both deals show a spelling mismatch between the deal name and the actual company name, which will break name-based reporting, search, and any downstream join that assumes deal name reflects company name.\r\n      [hubspot.search 09536e3d, hubspot.companies e89a9b89, hubspot.companies cd446a09, hubspot.companies 8dfac3d8]\r\n  P\u2588 Audit imported deals (source_detail = IMPORT) for missing engagement history and backfill or annotate them, since these deals will otherwise appear to have had no sales activity in any activity-based reporting or attribution analysis.\r\n      why: The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal, the only one of the four tagged IMPORT, is also the only one with zero logged engagements, despite being the largest deal in the quarter by dollar amount and contact count.\r\n      [hubspot.closed_won 22826304, hubspot.activities c974603c]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The activity history for the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 account (\u2588\u2588 rows) was seen only as a digest \u2014 timestamp range, type counts, and top summary strings \u2014 not read in full. Any claim about the specific content or completeness of individual engagements in that history beyond what the digest reports (\u2588\u2588 emails on 2026-09-15, type breakdown of \u2588\u2588 emails/\u2588 calls/\u2588 meetings/\u2588 note) is not verified.\r\n  - Company search results were capped and one search (\"\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\") returned only \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 total matching records even after reading the full digest; the \u2588\u2588 unread company records could contain further duplicates or the specific record actually linked to the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal, which was never confirmed by ID.\r\n  - No deal-to-company association ID was directly queried for any of the four deals; company matches were inferred by name search only, so the mismatches identified (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/JCT) are strong textual evidence but not a confirmed broken foreign-key link in the CRM schema.\r\n  - The zero-engagement finding for the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal's company record covers only that one company ID; it is possible engagements are logged against a different, duplicate \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record (the search found two records named '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588') rather than truly absent for the account.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- findings[0].claims[1]: The searches confirm zero closed-won deals lack amount or owner in the window, but the evidence contains no reference to 'four deals' specifically, so that count is unverified.\r\n- findings[3].claims[0]: The activities query used object_id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 with object_type companies, but \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 is actually the deal ID per evidence two, not a company ID, so the zero-activities resul\r\n- findings[3].claims[2]: The source_detail values are correctly reported (IMPORT vs CRM_UI/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/organic-search), but the evidence contains no information about the CRM's engagement-logging workflow,\r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. The observations show the \u2588 closed-won deals this quarter, confirm no missing amount/owner fields, and surface one naming inconsistency (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 vs \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) plus company duplication (multiple \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company records). This is descriptive detail, not a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588atic audit of CRM trustworthiness, and doesn't establish whether these are isolated issues or symptomatic of broader data problems. What would settle it: Per-deal field-completeness audit across a broader property set (contract dates, deal_type consistency, close reasons) rather than just amount/owner presence checks; Comparison against source \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-of-record (e.g., signed contract dates vs CRM close_date) to check for backdating or sync lag; Historical baseline of data quality in prior quarters to know if current gaps are a change or status quo; Ex\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Core deal fields (amount, owner) are complete for all closed-won deals in this quarter's window per direct queries; the data-quality problems found are in company-record linkage and activity-history completeness, not in the deal object's own required fields.\r\n  - One activity-history observation (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588 rows) was retrieved but only its digest was reviewed, not the full row-level data; findings about it are limited to what the digest reports.\r\n  - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company search truncated at \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 total matching records; the digest covers all \u2588\u2588 but individual unread rows beyond the \u2588\u2588 shown were not inspected.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - \u2588 of the \u2588\u2588 cited observation(s) returned no results (hubspot.activities, hubspot.companies). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  c974603c  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/REDACTED/engagements\r\n  290ff245  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/REDACTED/engagements\r\n  10f35c7d  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/REDACTED/engagements\r\n  22826304  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2026-07-01..2026-09-23\r\n  80c39f4d  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  a184977d  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  e89a9b89  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  8dfac3d8  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  cd446a09  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  09536e3d  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  2c62f3ea  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!amount?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  7401f383  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!hubspot_owner_id?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (138s wall, 136s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1      1.0    1%     1.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      4.2    3%     4.2  in 0 out 0\r\n  loop_model       7     48.6   35%     6.9  in 14 out 3,931 cached 152,761\r\n  loop_tools       6     19.1   14%     3.2  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     45.7   33%    45.7  in 38,303 out 4,849\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1     11.4    8%    11.4  in 34,705 out 1,582\r\n  sufficiency      1      6.0    4%     6.0  in 8,710 out 354\r\n  unmeasured              2.4    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 65%\r\n"]
